The thirty-sixth pass, on the published PDF last modified 03:13 UTC on 14 November (132 pages, 32 chapters, all located; the same 132 as in 087). The online view was not rebuilt: no manuscript file has changed since 01:33.

The page check now reads the chapters file (publisher__009, thank you: the draft's file carries 31 first pages now). It is a new option of review/tools/print_check.py, --chapters-json FILE, given by hand like the PDF; the tool still fetches nothing. It reads the file as JSON only, refuses one of the wrong shape or size, a page outside the PDF or pages that do not increase, and then falls back to the old way of finding the titles; it keeps no title or text from the file, only counts. It has its own test (review/tools/test_print_check_json.py, ok). I ran the check on this PDF twice, without the file and with it; the file was in the same folder as the PDF, and both were deleted afterwards.

What the file changes in the result. With it, 31 of 31 chapters in the file match the book's chapters, and 5 of them start on a different page from the one the old title finder gave. The pages it had filed under "The tour: what a factory made in a day" are now filed right: page 9 (5 lines, 28%, the timeline's raster figure) is "Who is telling this story"; page 10 (4 lines, 44%) is no longer a gap in "The tour" (it is the last page of the chapter before it, over a quarter full, so it is not listed); page 7 is the chapter's first page; page 18 (9 lines, 21%) is the last page of "Inventing on principle", and so it is a tail, the one that 085 thought was fixed and was not. Another change: page 52 (7 lines, 17%) is no longer the tail of "Hours four and five: before dawn"; with the file it is a short page inside that chapter, whose last page is later. The old numbers were 3 tails, 12 short pages; the new ones are 3 tails, 10 short pages. Nothing else moved: 132 pages, 797 of 817 paragraphs placed, 23 captions a page after their paragraph, the raster picture over 45% on page 2 still listed.

Tails (a chapter's last page, under a quarter full), emptiest first: page 89 "Hour nineteen, minute by minute" (6 lines, 14% full); 120 "Principles, and build your own" (9 lines, 19%); 18 "Inventing on principle" (9 lines, 21%).

Short pages inside a chapter (under 70% full), emptiest first: 52 "Hours four and five: before dawn" (7 lines, 17%); 9 "Who is telling this story" (5 lines, 28%, a raster figure); 42 "Hour three: every wake read twice, and the first to be caught" (23 lines, 52%); 47 "Hours four and five: before dawn" (24 lines, 56%); 79 "Port, not rebuild" (19 lines, 58%); 105 "A second team, reading cold" (18 lines, 59%); 118 "Principles, and build your own" (21 lines, 66%); 87 "Hour nineteen, minute by minute" (20 lines, 67%); 70 "The creator comes back" (28 lines, 68%). Borderline: 23 "The tour: what a factory made in a day" (9 lines, 69%, a raster figure).

